{"id": "EUVD-2026-102288", "enisaUuid": "94036b1c-f5f4-311b-97b9-0f754b09c310", "description": "libADLMIDI 1.6.2 through 1.6.2.1 contains an off-by-one stack out-of-bounds write vulnerability in BW_MidiSequencer that allows attackers to corrupt stack memory via crafted MIDI files. Attackers can supply a MIDI file with a note-on using status 0x9F and note 0x7F through adl_openFile() or adl_openData() to crash the hosting media player or game engine.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:33:17", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libadlmidi-notestates-note-index-stack-oob", "https://github.com/Wohlstand/libADLMIDI/blob/99c5e03a5cf9b4fdf35b53efddb853c96320d50f/src/midiseq/impl/read_smf_impl.hpp#L113", "https://github.com/Wohlstand/libADLMIDI/blob/99c5e03a5cf9b4fdf35b53efddb853c96320d50f/src/midiseq/impl/miditrack_impl.hpp#L350-L357", "https://github.com/Wohlstand/libADLMIDI", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libadlmidi-1.6.2-through-1.6.2.1-stack-out-of-bounds-write-via-bw-midisequencer-notestates"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rxj4-pqxj-5j52", "CVE-2026-111161"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6f8249ab-8713-31b2-960a-1774b880667f", "product": {"name": "libADLMIDI", "vendor": {"name": "Wohlstand"}}, "product_version": "1.6.2 \u22641.6.2.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "550ffc77-c0c8-3d12-ab90-b8a0aaa941d3", "vendor": {"name": "Wohlstand"}}], "isExploited": false}